# Prettier is scoped to the frontend workspace.
#
# `make format` already runs it from `frontend/`, and no CI job verifies its
# output anywhere in this repository. Outside that workspace every file is
# hand-authored — the documentation corpus is hard-wrapped prose with
# blockquote-heavy delivery records, and prettier's Markdown printer rewrites
# it: it joins blockquote lines onto the preceding one, drops the `>` from
# continuation lines, and reads the `*` inside a code span as an emphasis
# marker. It silently turned `/api/v1/*` into `/api/v1/_` in
# docs/roadmap/phase-01-repository-tooling.md.
#
# This file is what stops the editor. `.vscode/settings.json` maps `[markdown]`
# to the Prettier extension, which honours `.prettierignore` from the workspace
# root — so ignoring here covers both format-on-save and an explicit
# Format Document. The pre-commit hook runs prettier with `frontend/` as its
# working directory, where this file does not apply, so it carries the same
# boundary as a path filter of its own.

/*
!/frontend/
